45
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:11,480
Tanabe, did you read that article?

46
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:13,990
Yeah. Isn't that something?

47
00:03:13,990 --> 00:03:16,060
The first batter up,
and in the major league, too!

48
00:03:16,060 --> 00:03:18,360
Yeah...

49
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:19,930
The way our lives have been,

50
00:03:19,930 --> 00:03:22,430
we'll never be able to write
an interesting autobiography.

51
00:03:22,430 --> 00:03:24,100
Hey, Tanaka...

52
00:03:24,100 --> 00:03:26,930
Are you living your life
to write an autobiography?

53
00:03:26,930 --> 00:03:30,370
Of course not. But...

54
00:03:30,370 --> 00:03:33,940
Let's enjoy life! C'mon!

55
00:03:33,940 --> 00:03:34,970
Hey, Tanabe!

56
00:03:34,970 --> 00:03:38,040
-C'mon, Yoshida-kun!
-Have you gained weight, Kazuko?

57
00:03:38,040 --> 00:03:41,050
Listen, I shortened my
100-meter time by two seconds!

58
00:03:41,050 --> 00:03:43,380
I found this great shaved ice shop.
Why don't we go?

59
00:03:43,380 --> 00:03:45,850
Don't splash me!

60
00:03:47,150 --> 00:03:49,060
Oh, this is great!

61
00:03:49,060 --> 00:03:51,120
This is good! It's good! It's good!

62
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:55,230
Oh! It's Ishiguro-sempai!

63
00:03:55,230 --> 00:03:57,760
A beautiful face and dynamite body!

64
00:03:57,760 --> 00:04:01,270
A great athlete and her grades
are always in the top ten!

65
00:04:01,270 --> 00:04:04,070
Izumi Ishiguro's the perfect
Miss Higashi Middle School!

66
00:04:04,070 --> 00:04:06,970
She gets me hot all over! I can't stand it!

67
00:04:06,970 --> 00:04:08,810
-You're next!
-Okay!

68
00:04:08,810 --> 00:04:12,380
Okay...I'm gonna snap away...

69
00:04:12,380 --> 00:04:14,710
I'll sell 'em all and make me a fortune!

70
00:04:17,550 --> 00:04:20,490
Hey! What are you doing?!

71
00:04:21,320 --> 00:04:25,550
I see. You want to take some too?
Is that it?

72
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:43,740
Back then, Izumi-chain was
the first person to talk to me.

73
00:04:48,050 --> 00:04:51,850
"Thank you for your years of patronage.
Nakajima Calligraphy School"
"Tenant Wanted"

74
00:05:20,410 --> 00:05:22,320
-Izumi-chan...
-Give it back!

75
00:05:22,320 --> 00:05:25,810
Until three years ago,
that's what I called her.

76
00:05:26,790 --> 00:05:28,860
Someone's over there!

77
00:05:28,860 --> 00:05:32,850
See?! There are two guys over there!

78
00:05:37,660 --> 00:05:41,400
Who are they?! 7th graders?!

79
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:43,160
Somebody you know, Izumi?

80
00:05:46,140 --> 00:05:48,910
-They had a camera, those two.
-Catch them!

81
00:05:48,910 --> 00:05:50,540
Koyuki?

82
00:05:52,750 --> 00:05:56,650
Man, they got a good look at us.

83
00:05:56,650 --> 00:05:59,420
Come on. Let's go to the game center.

84
00:05:59,420 --> 00:06:01,440
Hurry up, Tanaka!

85
00:06:05,990 --> 00:06:08,550
Hey, stop that!

86
00:06:11,060 --> 00:06:12,370
Get lost!

87
00:06:12,370 --> 00:06:14,300
Yeah, that's it! Go!

88
00:06:17,540 --> 00:06:19,030
Thanks!

89
00:06:33,390 --> 00:06:36,180
Did it! The Golden Bat!

90
00:06:38,730 --> 00:06:42,030
-Wanna eat a beef bowl?
-I'll pass. I'm broke.

91
00:06:42,030 --> 00:06:44,500
I see. See ya!

92
00:06:51,900 --> 00:06:54,430
This place seems a little iffy...

93
00:06:58,910 --> 00:07:00,510
Whaddya want?!

94
00:07:00,510 --> 00:07:02,570
Ouch...

95
00:07:06,950 --> 00:07:09,220
Oww...

96
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:11,820
Man...

97
00:07:13,530 --> 00:07:15,430
What am I doing?

98
00:07:21,070 --> 00:07:22,590
Oww!

99
00:07:23,970 --> 00:07:26,110
Yay! Now it's my turn! Hold him!

100
00:07:26,110 --> 00:07:29,540
You can't get away from us!

101
00:07:29,540 --> 00:07:31,440
Wait!

102
00:07:33,050 --> 00:07:34,670
Damn!

103
00:07:36,450 --> 00:07:39,490
What's with that dog?!

104
00:07:39,490 --> 00:07:44,960
Hey, what are you doing?
Quit tormenting the dog!

105
00:07:44,960 --> 00:07:47,460
Aw, shut up! Let's get outta here!

106
00:07:47,460 --> 00:07:50,000
Yeah!

107
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:53,300
Beck! Come here!

108
00:07:53,300 --> 00:07:56,800
I told you, you shouldn't go out alone.

109
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:59,800
You...You made me worried.

110
00:08:01,110 --> 00:08:03,870
That guy's...a foreigner?

111
00:08:05,550 --> 00:08:07,280
Doesn't this dog look weird?

112
00:08:07,280 --> 00:08:10,280
No, no...Not bad dog...

113
00:08:10,280 --> 00:08:12,590
Huh? You're Japanese?

114
00:08:12,590 --> 00:08:15,820
Thanks for saving Beck.

115
00:08:15,820 --> 00:08:18,290
Doggy...Come here, doggy.

116
00:08:18,290 --> 00:08:20,780
Good boy...

117
00:08:22,830 --> 00:08:27,360
Uh-uh. You shouldn't put your hand out
to a frightened dog.

118
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:33,110
-Use these.
-Thanks.

119
00:08:33,110 --> 00:08:34,600
See ya.

120
00:08:38,010 --> 00:08:39,880
"Onochin Loans"
(This is a pack of tissues)

121
00:08:44,280 --> 00:08:47,310
I'll return this to you next time!

122
00:08:50,420 --> 00:08:51,820
Is that for real?

123
00:08:51,820 --> 00:08:56,450
Yeah. First I get punched,
and then I get bitten...What a day!

124
00:08:57,430 --> 00:09:00,130
No way...That's awful!

125
00:09:01,730 --> 00:09:07,070
That weird dog...I hope
it doesn't have rabies.

126
00:09:07,070 --> 00:09:09,380
Hey! There's someone here
to see you, Tanaka!

127
00:09:09,380 --> 00:09:12,110
It's Ishiguro-sempai!

128
00:09:14,610 --> 00:09:16,550
Uhh...Don't let them bother you.

129
00:09:16,550 --> 00:09:19,620
Listen, are you free on Saturday, Koyuki?

130
00:09:19,620 --> 00:09:20,780
Huh?!

131
00:09:23,320 --> 00:09:25,460
What happened? You get into a fight?

132
00:09:25,460 --> 00:09:28,490
It's nothing. I'm perfectly fine now.

133
00:09:28,490 --> 00:09:30,500
Listen, Koyuki...

134
00:09:30,500 --> 00:09:33,230
There was another boy
with the same name as me,

135
00:09:33,230 --> 00:09:35,370
Yukio Tanaka, in our calligraphy class.

136
00:09:35,370 --> 00:09:38,940
So Izumi-chan gave me
the nickname Koyuki.
(Ko = little)

137
00:09:38,940 --> 00:09:41,170
That's why she calls me Koyuki.

138
00:09:41,170 --> 00:09:42,140
"Koyuki"
That's why she calls me Koyuki.

139
00:09:42,140 --> 00:09:43,040
"Koyuki"

140
00:09:43,610 --> 00:09:48,580
I'm going bowling with some friends.
Won't you come with us?

141
00:09:48,580 --> 00:09:49,450
Yeah...

142
00:09:49,450 --> 00:09:52,450
Oh, good. Now we have enough people.

143
00:09:52,450 --> 00:09:56,460
It's almost exam time, so it's
hard getting everyone to join in.

144
00:09:56,460 --> 00:10:00,290
I didn't want to waste
the coupon Kayo-chan gave me.

145
00:10:01,460 --> 00:10:03,430
Koyuki...Thanks.

146
00:10:03,430 --> 00:10:04,730
Yeah...

147
00:10:04,730 --> 00:10:08,530
Oh, I have P.E. Next. See you Saturday!

148
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:13,040
I can't believe it...

149
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:14,970
You're telling me...

150
00:10:24,450 --> 00:10:27,690
-You seem to be happy.
-Yeah, well...

151
00:10:27,690 --> 00:10:30,320
-Don't stay out too late, now!
-I won't.

152
00:10:31,790 --> 00:10:35,360
The uptown-bound train
will be pulling in to track two.

153
00:10:35,360 --> 00:10:39,330
Please wait behind the yellow line.

154
00:10:39,330 --> 00:10:41,360
Wait behind the yellow line!

155
00:10:43,770 --> 00:10:46,610
Yay! I got a strike!

156
00:10:46,610 --> 00:10:48,400
Nice, Izumi-chan!

157
00:10:57,980 --> 00:11:00,190
We'll never win at this rate!

158
00:11:00,190 --> 00:11:03,690
Come on, Izumi. Let's switch teams.

159
00:11:03,690 --> 00:11:05,160
Koyuki...

160
00:11:07,730 --> 00:11:10,660
Try aiming at those marks in front of you.

161
00:11:21,210 --> 00:11:23,440
Yay! Alright!

162
00:11:23,440 --> 00:11:25,380
Pretty good advice, don't you think?

163
00:11:25,380 --> 00:11:27,710
Oh, no. It's me...My talent.

164
00:11:27,710 --> 00:11:29,280
Yay!

165
00:11:29,280 --> 00:11:31,150
You're pretty good, Koyuki!

166
00:11:33,050 --> 00:11:34,990
-Yes!
-Good job!

167
00:11:34,990 --> 00:11:38,620
At that moment, the two years
we hadn't seen each other...

168
00:11:38,620 --> 00:11:40,560
...vanished completely.

169
00:11:50,300 --> 00:11:52,070
Boy, am I hungry!

170
00:11:52,070 --> 00:11:54,740
-Let's go to McDonald's!
-How about Mr. Donut?

171
00:11:54,740 --> 00:11:56,510
I'd rather have a Yoshinoya beef bowl.

172
00:11:56,510 --> 00:11:58,340
-Huh?!
-Huh?!
-Huh?!

173
00:11:58,340 --> 00:12:00,510
What do I want?

174
00:12:00,510 --> 00:12:03,980
I'll go by myself...

175
00:12:03,980 --> 00:12:06,790
Oh! Kayo-chan!

176
00:12:06,790 --> 00:12:08,190
Kayo-chan!

177
00:12:08,190 --> 00:12:10,690
Oh, Izumichi!

178
00:12:10,690 --> 00:12:12,730
Yeah!

179
00:12:12,730 --> 00:12:13,930
What are you doing?

180
00:12:13,930 --> 00:12:17,430
We're trying to decide whether
to go to McDonald's or Yoshinoya.

181
00:12:17,430 --> 00:12:18,630
McDonald's!

182
00:12:18,630 --> 00:12:21,970
I'm not hungry. Let's go somewhere else.

183
00:12:21,970 --> 00:12:24,400
Kayo-chan, you're reeking of alcohol...

184
00:12:29,840 --> 00:12:33,510
-I hear it's pretty good.
-No way...

185
00:12:35,110 --> 00:12:36,910
Oh, come on...

186
00:12:49,030 --> 00:12:50,500
Yay!

187
00:12:55,170 --> 00:12:57,640
Are you drinking, Koyuki-kun?

188
00:12:57,640 --> 00:13:02,370
Yes. I'm on my second glass
of oolong tea.

189
00:13:02,370 --> 00:13:04,780
Shall we all go for karaoke?

190
00:13:04,780 --> 00:13:09,850
I'll pass. I've never been to a
karaoke place, and I'm out of money.

191
00:13:09,850 --> 00:13:13,790
But Izumichi was raving
about your singing...

192
00:13:13,790 --> 00:13:15,960
Here you go! It's on the house, kids!

193
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:19,290
Oh, Mit-chan...Did you
have a chef's license?

194
00:13:19,290 --> 00:13:20,760
'Course not.

195
00:13:27,700 --> 00:13:32,340
-What's Mit-chan-san's real name?
-Why?

196
00:13:32,340 --> 00:13:33,840
I want to thank him,

197
00:13:33,840 --> 00:13:37,280
but I don't think a kid like me
should be calling him Mit-chan...

198
00:13:37,280 --> 00:13:40,210
Why, I don't mind you calling me Mit-chan.

199
00:13:41,210 --> 00:13:44,180
Thanks for the food, Mit-chan-san!

200
00:13:44,180 --> 00:13:47,120
You know, we have a lot of regulars,

201
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:49,590
but none of them knows
what the others do.

202
00:13:49,590 --> 00:13:53,390
They don't even know if their names
are real or just nicknames.

203
00:13:53,390 --> 00:13:57,890
It's Remedy's policy not
to bring problems in here.

204
00:14:01,870 --> 00:14:04,300
But that means you're breaking up with me!

205
00:14:04,300 --> 00:14:07,600
As I said, I don't have the time.

206
00:14:10,080 --> 00:14:12,480
Oh, man...

207
00:14:12,480 --> 00:14:14,550
Damn you, Ryusuke...

208
00:14:14,550 --> 00:14:18,520
He's called Ryusuke. Mature for 16.

209
00:14:18,520 --> 00:14:21,790
-You know him?
-Uhh...no...

210
00:14:21,790 --> 00:14:27,090
He's the worst...Making girls cry,
not paying back money he owes...

211
00:14:27,090 --> 00:14:28,650
No way...

212
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:31,630
But, how can I put it?

213
00:14:31,630 --> 00:14:37,090
He has a strange attraction
for other people, that Ryusuke.

214
00:14:38,240 --> 00:14:42,940
-Besides, he's always bluffing.
-Mit-chan, sake!

215
00:14:42,940 --> 00:14:44,980
Bluffing?

216
00:14:44,980 --> 00:14:47,410
Koyuki, have you heard of Dying Breed?

217
00:14:48,880 --> 00:14:54,080
There's this super popular band
called Dying Breed in America.

218
00:14:55,050 --> 00:15:00,190
What about Dying Breed? I love them!

219
00:15:00,190 --> 00:15:04,630
He says he used to play in a band
with Eddy, Dying Breed's guitarist.

220
00:15:13,410 --> 00:15:15,460
Who are you talking about?

221
00:15:17,180 --> 00:15:19,580
You idiot...

222
00:15:19,580 --> 00:15:23,240
Come on. You've got
other guys besides me.

223
00:15:25,150 --> 00:15:30,250
Ryusuke! Which is more important
to you?! Me or the band?!

224
00:15:31,320 --> 00:15:32,850
The band.

225
00:15:39,030 --> 00:15:42,740
Mit-chan-san...Would you give this to him?

226
00:15:42,740 --> 00:15:43,830
Sure...

227
00:15:47,110 --> 00:15:50,380
Wasn't it like a drama back there?

228
00:15:50,380 --> 00:15:52,910
Yeah. It was really something.

229
00:15:52,910 --> 00:15:54,450
Hey!

230
00:15:54,450 --> 00:15:57,980
Hey! Hey! Come look at this!

231
00:15:57,980 --> 00:16:01,320
Somebody really did a job on this car.

232
00:16:01,320 --> 00:16:04,190
It's gonna cost a mint to fix it.

233
00:16:04,190 --> 00:16:07,760
Sempai, I don't think
you should get too close.

234
00:16:07,760 --> 00:16:10,060
What is it? Killjoy.

235
00:16:10,060 --> 00:16:15,030
Hey! What the fuck are
you doing to my car?!

236
00:16:15,030 --> 00:16:19,770
Whatsa matter, you fuckers around
here speak English, or what?

237
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:22,440
Oh...I'm...sorry...

238
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:24,540
Sempai! Why are you apologizing?!

239
00:16:24,540 --> 00:16:26,570
W-well...

240
00:16:33,720 --> 00:16:36,240
-You leaving?
-Yeah...

241
00:16:37,260 --> 00:16:40,660
A young kid asked me to give this to you.

242
00:16:40,660 --> 00:16:44,820
To me? Thanks, Mit-chan.

243
00:16:46,630 --> 00:16:48,030
Fuckin' stupid little kids!

244
00:16:48,030 --> 00:16:50,970
I'm gonna make you pay
for all of this right now!

245
00:16:50,970 --> 00:16:55,170
No, no. We are not guilty. We-

246
00:16:56,240 --> 00:17:00,850
What are you, a rapper or a singer?
"We are the world?!"

247
00:17:00,850 --> 00:17:04,850
I'll kick your ass if you don't pay!
I'm serious. Shut the...

248
00:17:04,850 --> 00:17:06,590
...fuck up!

249
00:17:06,590 --> 00:17:09,020
Back off, damn you!

250
00:17:09,020 --> 00:17:09,990
Koyuki...

251
00:17:09,990 --> 00:17:13,320
Don't act big just because
you're overgrown, dumbass (baka yaro)!

252
00:17:14,760 --> 00:17:17,190
Ba...ka?

253
00:17:18,960 --> 00:17:21,230
Nobody calls me baka around here!

254
00:17:21,230 --> 00:17:24,340
You little shit! I'm kicking
your fucking ass, man! Right about now!

255
00:17:24,340 --> 00:17:26,770
Stop it!

256
00:17:26,770 --> 00:17:30,940
I saw your car two hours ago
and it was already scratched.

257
00:17:30,940 --> 00:17:33,540
Who the hell are you?!

258
00:17:35,880 --> 00:17:38,580
You should apologize to these kids.

259
00:17:38,580 --> 00:17:40,850
What the fuck?!

260
00:17:40,850 --> 00:17:42,550
Apologize.

261
00:17:44,720 --> 00:17:46,090
Apologize!

262
00:17:49,460 --> 00:17:51,130
The police are right there.

263
00:17:51,130 --> 00:17:53,330
Shut the fuck up, kid!

264
00:17:53,330 --> 00:17:55,600
Here, let's get somewhere else.

265
00:17:57,270 --> 00:17:58,800
Come on!

266
00:17:58,800 --> 00:18:00,290
Come on, he says...

267
00:18:03,280 --> 00:18:05,480
Ryusuke-kun!

268
00:18:05,480 --> 00:18:07,450
Never mind me. Get on home.

269
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:12,480
"Noodles"

270
00:18:12,480 --> 00:18:14,790
"Noodles"

271
00:18:12,480 --> 00:18:14,790
Here are your ramen noodles.

272
00:18:14,790 --> 00:18:16,850
"Noodles"

273
00:18:14,790 --> 00:18:16,850
This looks good!

274
00:18:17,820 --> 00:18:22,590
But those French fries...
Weren't they just awful?

275
00:18:27,300 --> 00:18:30,000
You haven't finished your ramen.

276
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:36,040
Yeah...But I really want
to eat a beef bowl!

277
00:18:36,040 --> 00:18:37,670
Koyuki...

278
00:18:58,260 --> 00:19:02,470
Hey, hey-hey hey!
I-It's cool, man. It's cool.

279
00:19:02,470 --> 00:19:04,900
Put that thing down, man, please.

280
00:19:04,900 --> 00:19:07,070
Put it down. Take it easy.

281
00:19:07,070 --> 00:19:07,940
Please...

282
00:19:07,940 --> 00:19:10,810
Well...Wanna try?

283
00:19:10,810 --> 00:19:16,980
I don't know about your town,
but my friends in New York died.

284
00:19:16,980 --> 00:19:20,290
You can't fuck around in my neighborhood.

285
00:19:20,290 --> 00:19:23,060
Get the fuck outta here! Fucking bastard!

286
00:19:23,060 --> 00:19:25,550
-No! No! Leave it!
-Don't shoot! Don't shoot!

287
00:19:31,360 --> 00:19:33,090
Ryusuke-kun!

288
00:19:35,370 --> 00:19:38,930
Damn...Treating me like trash...

289
00:19:40,170 --> 00:19:42,370
Shit!

290
00:19:42,370 --> 00:19:44,410
R-Ryusuke-kun! Are you all right?!

291
00:19:44,410 --> 00:19:48,650
They were so drunk, I didn't
think they'd figure it out.

292
00:19:48,650 --> 00:19:51,050
Man...it hurts...

293
00:19:53,620 --> 00:19:56,260
I was impressed.

294
00:19:56,260 --> 00:20:01,490
You're such a shorty, but you
went after those big foreigners.

295
00:20:01,490 --> 00:20:03,730
What's the matter?

296
00:20:03,730 --> 00:20:06,990
Hey, hey...I'm the one
who should be crying.

297
00:20:08,770 --> 00:20:13,410
I'm sorry. But lately...
for a long time, actually,

298
00:20:13,410 --> 00:20:18,780
I felt like no one cared if I lived or not.

299
00:20:18,780 --> 00:20:20,300
Koyuki!

300
00:20:23,050 --> 00:20:24,740
It's them...

301
00:20:29,120 --> 00:20:30,190
Hey, you guys-

302
00:20:30,190 --> 00:20:33,990
-Are you all right?
-I'm just scratched up.

303
00:20:33,990 --> 00:20:36,730
The other day, he saved my dog.

304
00:20:36,730 --> 00:20:38,100
Your dog?

305
00:20:38,100 --> 00:20:42,370
Beck is a dog Eddy and I found
when we were in a band together.

306
00:20:42,370 --> 00:20:45,770
-Oh, so that's a true story?
-Oh, sorry Koyuki-kun.

307
00:20:45,770 --> 00:20:49,830
-Sorry I'm so late.
-Yeah...

308
00:20:51,340 --> 00:20:54,080
I love the Dying Breed!

309
00:20:54,080 --> 00:20:57,450
Oh? Then why don't you come
and see our band sometime?

310
00:20:57,450 --> 00:21:00,350
Yes! I will! That's so exciting!

311
00:21:00,350 --> 00:21:02,750
Matt of Dying Breed is really funny.

312
00:21:02,750 --> 00:21:06,660
If he doesn't have a drink before
a show he can't get up on the stage.

313
00:21:15,970 --> 00:21:18,160
That looks pretty weird to me.

314
00:21:20,040 --> 00:21:25,110
Now I'm pretty worried...
for Ishiguro-sempai.

315
00:21:25,110 --> 00:21:27,940
I don't give a damn about you, though.

316
00:21:33,220 --> 00:21:39,650
So cheer up...

317
00:21:40,630 --> 00:21:42,460
Sorry to keep you waiting!

318
00:21:44,630 --> 00:21:46,800
This is Ryusuke-kun's address...

319
00:21:46,800 --> 00:21:48,970
Okay...Shall we barge in on him?

320
00:21:48,970 --> 00:21:51,460
Huh? Right now?

321
00:21:57,640 --> 00:22:01,780
Koyuki...What kind of music
do you listen to?

322
00:22:01,780 --> 00:22:06,250
-Chiemi Kuniyoshi.
-Kuniyoshi? Oh, that idol singer?

323
00:22:06,250 --> 00:22:10,550
Yeah...I'm sure she's going
to break out soon.

324
00:22:17,060 --> 00:22:19,700
I think it's this way.

325
00:22:19,700 --> 00:22:21,330
Maybe...

326
00:22:21,330 --> 00:22:25,070
And, after taking a lot of wrong turns,

327
00:22:25,070 --> 00:22:27,630
we finally arrived at Ryusuke-kun's home.

328
00:22:31,940 --> 00:22:41,220
"Fishing"

329
00:22:51,260 --> 00:22:53,360
Another minute

330
00:22:53,360 --> 00:22:56,190
Feelin' so fine

331
00:22:58,360 --> 00:23:00,600
You turn the freeze

332
00:23:00,600 --> 00:23:03,230
into warm light

333
00:23:05,440 --> 00:23:09,010
Had a premonition

334
00:23:09,010 --> 00:23:11,710
I've been waitin' ever since

335
00:23:11,710 --> 00:23:14,200
My world comin' down

336
00:23:15,210 --> 00:23:17,770
It's got me spinnin' 'round

337
00:23:19,780 --> 00:23:26,120
If you really wanna fly

338
00:23:26,120 --> 00:23:28,890
you gotta let go

339
00:23:40,970 --> 00:23:43,310
Simply the most

340
00:23:43,310 --> 00:23:45,340
big sensation

341
00:23:45,340 --> 00:23:48,150
(once you're here you won't go back)

342
00:23:48,150 --> 00:23:50,420
She's really pretty

343
00:23:50,420 --> 00:23:52,750
One-eyed vision

344
00:23:52,750 --> 00:23:55,250
(lose the fear it don't come back)

345
00:23:55,250 --> 00:23:58,920
Little sister showed me

346
00:23:58,920 --> 00:24:01,560
Really took me for a ride

347
00:24:01,560 --> 00:24:03,160
My world comin' down

348
00:24:03,160 --> 00:24:06,630
(once you're here you won't go back)

349
00:24:06,630 --> 00:24:10,860
(lose the fear it don't come back)

350
00:24:14,470 --> 00:24:17,180
Rock, you see, is the
vibration of the soul. Hm?

351
00:24:17,180 --> 00:24:20,210
"Next Episode"

352
00:24:17,180 --> 00:24:20,210
Rock, you see, is the
vibration of the soul. Hm?

353
